The Tale of Genji associates each chapter from 2 to 53 with one of the 52 partitions of a 5-element set (the Bell number B_5 = 52), via the traditional Genji-kō diagrams. These diagrams depict five vertical incense sticks whose horizontal connections encode equality of scent, directly yielding the blocks of the corresponding set partition. The sticks are canonically numbered left-to-right as {1,2,3,4,5}.  

Given the supplied reference point that chapter 20 maps to the partition whose blocks are {1,3,4},{2},{5}, the same canonical ordering of diagrams assigns chapter 39 the partition whose blocks are {1,2,4},{3,5}. The blocks are written in increasing order of their minimal elements, satisfying the required output format.

