PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,4},{2,3,5}} 

The 52 Genji-kō patterns are exactly the set partitions of {1,2,3,4,5}, ordered by the lexicographic order of their restricted-growth representations (a1=1, ai between 1 and 1+max{a1..a_{i-1}}). Chapter c therefore corresponds to the (c-1)-st partition in that list.

The example given for chapter 20 is the 19th partition, whose RGF is (1,2,1,1,3) and whose blocks are {{1,3,4},{2},{5}}. Exactly 15 partitions have a2=1, so chapter 39 is the 23rd partition overall and therefore the 8th partition whose RGF begins (1,2,…). Enumeration of those RGFs shows that the desired entry is (1,2,2,1,2), whose blocks are {{1,4},{2,3,5}}.

