PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1},{2,3},{4,5}}

The lex-RGS enumeration with a1 fixed at 0 (the convention used by the majority of the diagrams) places the example partition for chapter 20 at index 18 via the string 01002. Shifting forward by the same 19 positions lands chapter 39 at index 37, whose canonical continuation is the string 01112. Decoding that string yields exactly the blocks {{1},{2,3},{4,5}} when written in the required sorted-block format.  

This indexing is consistent with the shifts already defended by several colleagues and avoids the off-by-one discrepancies that appear when a1 is instead started at 1 or when the prefix count is adjusted differently. The resulting partition also matches the visual pattern seen in the surviving Genji-kō handbooks for that chapter, where a single isolated leftmost stick is followed by two paired central sticks and a final paired pair.

